t. Much confusion in English results from the uncontrolled variations in me=
aning of these phrases and prefixes.</p>
 <p>In the examples of <a href=3D"../4/">Section 4</a>, we will translate t=
he general case of scalar negation using the general formula =93other than=
=94 when a phrase is scalar-negated, and =93non-=94 when a single word is s=
calar-negated.</p>
